Subject: Libretro: add mgba_dual_libretro, two GBAs on one lockstep link cable
Series-Step: 6/19 (mgba_dual 1.6-os4)
Origin: hanbang (this project), new files under src/platform/libretro/dual/ (MPL-2.0)
요약: 같은 롬 GBA 두 대를 한 libretro 코어 안에서 lockstep 케이블로 이어 돌리는 새 앞단(mgba_dual_libretro). 넷플레이로 두 기기가 입력만 주고받음.

New LIBRETRO_DUAL CMake option builds a separate frontend
(src/platform/libretro/dual/libretro_dual.c) that owns two GBA cores of
the same ROM and one GBASIOLockstepCoordinator. retro_run steps the
awake cores cooperatively until player 1 finishes a frame, so plain
RetroArch netplay drives the pair: port 0 -> 1P, port 1 -> 2P.

- savestates hold both cores, both lockstep driver blobs, both save
  buffers and the FIFO/DMA state the GBA serializer drops
- 1P save is the normal .srm, 2P save is <rom>.p2.srm (host only)
- core option mgba_dual_screen picks whose screen and audio are shown
- RTC uses a fixed epoch so both netplay peers stay deterministic

---
